---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

// No hero image: see PROCESS.md for why this course is image-free by
// design. ContentLayout renders a plain heading when heroImage is omitted.
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    On day one you pick one restaurant that has actually closed — not a
    chain closure, not a rumour, a specific address with a specific "sorry
    we're closed" sign — and you spend the rest of the semester on nothing
    else. Every week hands you a different instrument to point at it:
    location economics one week, the menu read like a balance sheet the
    next, the star-rating history plotted against time the week after that.
    You leave with a single finished autopsy report and a verdict you can
    defend under cross-examination, not a folder of unrelated exercises.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has ever watched a beloved restaurant disappear and wanted a
    better answer than "the rent went up." No hospitality or business
    background is assumed — the methods are taught from the specimen
    outward. What is assumed is that you can read a spreadsheet, sit through
    an uncomfortable disagreement about your own conclusions, and resist the
    first tidy story that explains the death.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The twelve-week case, one lens per week, in order.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>The dossier, the report and the inquest — what is marked and when.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who runs the inquest and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
